# REVISION-NEW-VISIT-PATIENT-SEARCH-COMBOBOX-1 — durable rules

Source of truth: `docs/sprints/revision-new-visit-patient-search-combobox-1.md`.
GO tag `revision-new-visit-patient-search-combobox-1-go`.

## 1. One control

"Kunjungan Baru" (`rme.visits.create`) selects a registered patient through
**exactly one** control: `<x-patient-combobox>`. There is no second dropdown, no
separate filter box, and no hidden native `<select name="patient_id">`. The only
`patient_id` field on the form is the component's hidden input.

Pinned by `NewVisitPatientSearchComboboxTest` — the rendered page must contain
`data-patient-combobox` and `name="patient_id"` exactly once each.

## 2. Server-side search only — never preload the patient set

`ClinicVisitController::create()` must NOT pass a patient collection to the view,
and no Blade template may iterate patients into `<option>` elements for this
control. The estate is not serialised into HTML.

Results come from `GET rme/visits/patient-search`
(`rme.visits.patient-search` → `ClinicVisitController::patientSearch`), gated by
the ClinicVisit `create` ability.

## 3. Branch scope — SUPERSEDED by rule 101

> **This section's original rule is no longer in force.** It required
> `PatientSelectorSearchService` to scope results to
> `RmeWorkingBranchScope::branchIdsFor()`, so a context-bound role searched only
> its own working branch. **REVISION-NEW-VISIT-GLOBAL-PATIENT-LOOKUP-1**
> deliberately replaced that with a GLOBAL patient identity lookup. See
> `.cursor/rules/101-new-visit-global-patient-identity-lookup.mdc`, which is the
> authority for the branch dimension of this control.

What survives from the original rule, unchanged and still binding:

- No valid working context ⇒ **empty** scope, empty results. Fail closed. Never
  a MAIN or first-branch fallback.
- Doctors are additionally narrowed by `DoctorPatientScopeService` (a CLINICAL
  scope, not a branch scope).
- Legacy patients with `branch_id` null stay selectable.
- Patients of non-RME / inactive branches are never selectable.
- The daily branch lock still owns mid-day working-branch moves. What changed is
  that the search no longer follows the working branch at all — it is global on
  both sides of an approved change.
- `RmeWorkingBranchScope` itself is NOT relaxed. It remains the canonical
  working-branch authority for every other surface; this control simply stopped
  using it as its identity boundary.

**The endpoint accepts no `branch_id` and no `limit`.** Do not add either. A
request value must never widen, narrow, re-point, or raise the scope or the
ceiling — and must never decide the branch a visit is created at.

## 4. Least disclosure

The search response carries exactly four keys:

```
id, name, medical_record_number, branch_label
```

Never phone, WhatsApp, KTP/NIK, address, date of birth, email, occupation, or
anything clinical. The test asserts the **exact key set**, so adding a field is a
deliberate act that must be argued, not a silent widening.

## 5. Bounded

`PatientSelectorSearchService::MIN_QUERY_LENGTH` (2) and `RESULT_LIMIT` (15) are
server constants. Below the minimum the server returns nothing — an empty or
one-character box can never become a patient dump. LIKE metacharacters in the
query are escaped, so a typed `%` matches literally.

## 6. Typed text is not a patient

`patient_id` is set **only** by explicitly selecting a returned result. Any
keystroke after a selection clears it. Switching to "Pasien Baru" clears it
(browser event `patient-selector-reset`, plus a server-side null in
`StoreClinicVisitRequest::prepareForValidation`, because a hidden panel still
submits its inputs).

## 7. A slower earlier response never wins

The combobox carries a monotonic request sequence and an AbortController. Every
`await` re-checks the sequence, so a late response for an older query is
discarded. This is unit-tested in `tests/js/patient-combobox.test.mjs`
(`npm run test:js`) — do not move the state machine back inline into `app.js`,
where it cannot be tested.

## 8. Visibility is not authorization

`StoreClinicVisitRequest` re-asserts the submitted `patient_id` through
`PatientSelectorSearchService::isSelectable()` — the **same** scope the search
uses, so what is selectable and what is submittable cannot drift apart. A crafted
id for a non-RME branch, for a nonexistent patient, or from an operator with no
valid working context is rejected even though the dropdown would never have
offered it. `Rule::exists` alone is not enough and must not be the only guard
again.

Under rule 101 a patient from **another RME branch** is a legitimate selection,
so it is accepted — but the check itself is untouched, and it never influences
the branch the visit is created at.

## 9. Do not conflate with the cross-branch RM lookup

`CrossBranchPatientLookupService` is the deliberate cross-branch **duplicate
detection** panel. It returns no patient id and must never become a selection
source. The two services stay separate.

## 10. Out of scope, deliberately

- The legacy `x-patient-search-select` component still serves the dental Lab
  Order form. It was not migrated here; that is a different page.
- Inactive patients remain selectable, exactly as before this revision.
